  "description": "## Status: NOT STARTED (analysis complete, ZERO files written)\n\nSub-agent of the exact-design-parity work, wound down before writing any code.\nBranch: feature/exact-design-parity\nWorktree: /Users/home/Projects/Anth.us-Papyrus-design (gitdir /Users/home/Projects/Anth.us-Papyrus/.git/worktrees/Anth.us-Papyrus-design)\n\n## Exact task\n\nCreate exactly two new files (touch nothing else in that repo):\n- web/anthus_page_html.py  -- GENERATED module holding the production <main> inner HTML\n- bin/extract-page-html.py -- auditable, repeatable extractor that WRITES that module; takes --anthus PATH (default ../Anth.us)\n\nReference: /Users/home/Projects/Anth.us/public/ (real Gatsby prod build, 2026-09-24, 243 pages). The emitted DOM must be the production DOM because the production stylesheet targets it. Leave hrefs, <mark>, index-module--*, platform-module--*, experience, resume, clear and every other class EXACTLY as-is.\n\nRequired public API:\n- about_html() -> str\n- ai_solutions_html(*, featured: str, portfolio: str, integrations: str) -> str\n- ryan_html(*, portfolio: str, integrations: str) -> str\n- not_found_html() -> str\n- set_image_renderer(render: ImageRenderer) -> None   (ImageRenderer = Callable[..., str]; module-level _render_image: ImageRenderer | None = None)\n- _image(name, alt, classes) -> str, calling _render_image(src=\"/assets/site/\"+name, alt=alt, class_name=classes, eager=True); RuntimeError if no renderer installed.\n\nCaller installs anthus_dom.image_html(*, src, alt=\"\", class_name=\"\", eager=False) -- CONFIRMED present at web/anthus_dom.py:260.\n\nEach function returns ONLY the inner HTML of <main> (not html/head/header/.wrapper/main/footer).\n\n## MEASURED FROM THE REFERENCE (reference-side only; no generated output exists)\n\n<main> inner HTML located as the span between '<main' ..'>' and '</main>'. Inner lengths and counts:\n- about/index.html        6291 chars; 0 gatsby-image blocks; 0 script/noscript; 1 <img>; 12 '<!-- -->'; 14 <mark>; 0 '/static/'\n- ai-solutions/index.html 53332 chars; 24 'gatsby-image-wrapper' hits; 8 <script> + 8 <noscript>; 34 <img>; 6 '<!-- -->'; 5 <mark>; 160 '/static/'\n- ryan/index.html         42784 chars; 15 'gatsby-image-wrapper' hits; 5 <script> + 5 <noscript>; 20 <img>; 5 '<!-- -->'; 12 <mark>\n- 404.html                   90 chars; fully static. Exact content:\n  <h1>404: Not Found</h1><p>You just hit a route that doesn&#x27;t exist... the sadness.</p>\n  (no <article> wrapper on 404, unlike the other three)\n\n### Hole spans (offsets into the <main> inner string)\n\n/ai-solutions/ -- exactly 3 top-level <ul class=\"index-module--list--fb407 ...\">, one per <h2>:\n- {featured}      2724..29851   smallImageList   items: B0rd, Speaker Role Classifier, Classification with Confidence, SQLBot: Your AI Database Analyst, Call Criteria\n- {portfolio}    29994..51062   smallImageList   items: Plexus, Ticketing Data Analysis, Vault, Ticket Driver Copilot, Store Driver, Ticket Driver, Menu Driver, Venue Driver, Checkout Driver\n- {integrations} 51083..53148   'undefined'      items: Paytronix, Salesforce Marketing Cloud, Salesforce, Marketo\n\n/ryan/ -- DEVIATION FROM THE BRIEF: there are THREE such <ul>s, not two.\n- 7305..34441  smallImageList, items B0rd..Call Criteria (the 'featured' set)\n- 34441..40682 'undefined',    items Plexus..Checkout Driver (the 'portfolio' set)\n  These two <ul>s are ADJACENT -- zero characters between them.\n- 40703..42768 'undefined',    items Paytronix..Marketo  -> {integrations}\nSince ryan_html() only takes portfolio= and integrations=, {portfolio} MUST span 7305..40682, i.e. BOTH adjacent lists, as one contiguous hole.\n\nRule that works for both pages: after the <h2>, match the first index-module--list--fb407 <ul> using <ul>/</ul> depth counting (these lists contain nested plain <ul>s -- ai-solutions at inner offsets 7539, 35690, 49744; ryan at 12121, 34913, 39364 -- so naive regex WILL be wrong), then keep extending while the text immediately following is another such <ul>. On ai-solutions nothing extends (an <h2> always follows). On ryan the portfolio hole absorbs both lists.\n\n### /ryan/ static skeleton (exact)\n'<article><div class=\"resume\">' + resume content + '<h2>Portfolio</h2>' + {portfolio} + '<h2>Integrations</h2>' + {integrations} + '</div></article>'\n(the integrations </ul> is immediately followed by '</div></article>')\n\n### ALL gatsby-plugin-image blocks and ALL scripts fall INSIDE the holes\nVerified by offset on both /ai-solutions/ and /ryan/. Consequence: the committed static HTML contains NO gatsby-image markup, NO <script>, NO <noscript>, NO '/static/' URLs. The extractor should still implement brief rules 2-4 and assert the counts, but those paths are no-ops for these four pages -- so they are effectively untested code. Consider running the transform over the full <main> (pre-hole-cut) as a self-check and asserting placeholder count == wrapper count.\n\n### Plain <img> surviving in static regions -- exactly 3\n- /about/ (inside the first <p>, immediately before 'In 2009,'):\n  <img src=\"/assets/images/ryan-porter.png\" alt=\"About Anthus\" class=\"responsive-float-right-image\"/>\n  -> _image(\"ryan-porter.png\", \"About Anthus\", \"responsive-float-right-image\")\n- /ai-solutions/ (immediately after <h1>Solving Problems Using AI</h1>):\n  <img src=\"/assets/images/ai-software-solutions.png\" alt=\"AI software solutions\" class=\"responsive-float-right-image\"/>\n  -> _image(\"ai-software-solutions.png\", \"AI software solutions\", \"responsive-float-right-image\")\n- /ai-solutions/ tail:\n  <h2>The Process</h2><figure><a href=\"https://plexus.anth.us\"><img src=\"/assets/images/Anthus AI Application Lifecycle.png\" alt=\"AI Application Lifecycle\"/></a></figure></div></article>\n  -> _image(\"Anthus AI Application Lifecycle.png\", \"AI Application Lifecycle\", \"\")\nNOTE: production srcs are /assets/images/..., NOT /static/<hash>/<hash>/... as the brief assumed. Basenames unchanged. All three basenames EXIST in web/assets/site/ (verified by ls).\n/ryan/ and /404 have ZERO images in their static regions, so ryan_html() and not_found_html() need no _image() calls at all.\n\n### Open design judgement for the next session\nProduction styles.04b540856f53bb5e70f2.css has:\n  .responsive-float-right-image{float:right;height:auto;margin-bottom:1em;margin-left:1em;width:40%}\nand in production that class is on the <img> ITSELF. anthus_dom.image_html() wraps the img in div.gatsby-image-wrapper.gatsby-image-wrapper-constrained and puts class_name on the WRAPPER. Routing these two images through _image() therefore changes the DOM shape (wrapper floats at 40%, inner img absolutely fills a sizer div). The brief explicitly asks for this ('the module must NOT hardcode image markup'; rule 3 covers responsive-float-right-image imgs) and it should be visually equivalent, but it is NOT byte-identical to production -- eyeball it in bin/compare.py output.\nThe <figure><a><img></a></figure> image has no class and its src is not /static/, so brief rules 3 and 4 do not clearly cover it. Decision taken (not implemented): also route it through _image(name, alt, \"\") so no image markup is hardcoded; this inserts a gatsby-image-wrapper inside the <a>. Revisit if the figure layout shifts.\n\n### Other extraction facts worth keeping\n- Removing React separators is a plain str.replace('<!-- -->', '') -- that preserves surrounding whitespace exactly. Do NOT regex it with \\s* on either side; 'foo<!-- --> <a>bar</a>' must keep its single space.\n- Static HTML contains literal curly braces in places, so str.format() over the whole document is unsafe. Plan: pure concatenation of committed constants + _image() calls + the hole arguments, plus a _no_holes(html) guard that raises if '{featured}', '{portfolio}' or '{integrations}' survives.\n- Adjacent Python string literals concatenate with no added whitespace, so breaking the long constants at block-tag boundaries is correctness-safe; it only affects reviewability. Never reflow inside text content.\n- /about/ mixes plain ASCII apostrophes (you're, Don't) with curly ones (doesn't). Keep bytes verbatim. Prefer single-quoted Python literals so HTML attribute double quotes need no escaping; fall back to double-quoted + escaping for chunks containing an apostrophe.\n- Keep hrefs exactly as-is (/ryan, /blog/call-criteria/, https://docs.google.com/forms/..., ...). A later build pass rewrites internal links.\n- Keep inline style=\"...\" attributes (/about/ 'Our Mission' <p> and the 'Our Values' <ul>/<li>/<p> all carry them) and the id=\"our-values\" on /about/'s second <h2>.\n- Note web/build_via_papyrus.py:442 scans built output for /assets/site/<name> references and asserts the files exist; _image() builds the src at runtime, so the static scan will only see the bare '/assets/site/' prefix in this module.\n\n## NOT DONE / NOT VERIFIED\n- bin/extract-page-html.py was never written.\n- web/anthus_page_html.py was never written.\n- No import check, no normalised diff vs reference, no class-token diff, no <mark>-count comparison of GENERATED output was run -- there is no generated output.\n- Every number above is a reference-side measurement.\n\n## Concrete next steps\n1. Write bin/extract-page-html.py: argparse --anthus (default ../Anth.us); per page extract <main> inner; find hole spans by the <h2> + run-of-adjacent-<ul> rule above; replace hole spans with sentinels; strip <script>/<noscript> elements wholesale; replace each 'div data-gatsby-image-wrapper' block by counting <div / </div> to the matching close, emitting {{IMAGE:basename|alt|classes}} (basename from the main <img>'s data-src or src; alt from its alt; classes = wrapper class list minus gatsby-image-wrapper and gatsby-image-wrapper-constrained); same placeholder form for plain <img>; rewrite any leftover /static/ src to /assets/site/<basename>; str.replace('<!-- -->',''); then emit the module with chunked adjacent string literals and turn each placeholder into an _image(...) call.\n2. Assert in the script: placeholder count == wrapper count; no '<script', '<noscript', 'gatsby-image-wrapper' or '/static/' remains in the emitted static HTML.\n3. Module docstring must say it is GENERATED by bin/extract-page-html.py from the four named reference pages, that it is the production DOM lifted verbatim because the production stylesheet targets it, what the dynamic holes are, and that it must be regenerated rather than hand-edited (hand-reviewed once after generation). No imports beyond typing, no import-time I/O, no network.\n4. Run the brief's verification: import check from repo root; per-page dummy-renderer round trip vs the reference normalised the same way (scripts + gatsby blocks stripped); class-token set diff; <mark> counts yours vs reference (expect about 14, ai-solutions 5, ryan 12, 404 0 -- but note marks inside the holes belong to the list renderer, not this module, so compare static regions only).",
